["er.eventlog.import-anchor/1",{"authority":{"logical_scope":"aep","stream_identity":"01a0d3bf-067c-7068-af65-bd964ce78fcb","tenant":"planning"},"completeness":"available_evidence_only","evidence":[],"instance":{"entity":"story","fields":{"body":"# Story: `aep eval run` refuses to spawn against a stale child `aep`\n\n## Outcome\n\nA live spawn is refused, before any money is spent, when the `aep` the session will execute is not the version that launched it; a case whose subject names an `ess-schema` skill is refused when the session has no `ess` to run.\n\n## Context\n\nmetaharness gives the session a constructed `PATH` — `home-path:sha256:bf0ce980507453a72ff552e629263aad96884f583e2ab5794252f4e5b2956f19` — and never the runner's own. On 2026-09-03 the golden-path case ran with a 0.40.1 copy in `home-path:sha256:8d6708581526e2954aab593f4ba61464fb67c0e06c88062276127839a99834b9` beside the 0.44.0 that launched it: step 3 was drafted by hand because `ess` was not there, and step 8 stopped at `aep doctor: unrecognized subcommand` after $10.96 had been spent. Nothing said the two binaries disagreed.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Before a live spawn the runner resolves `aep` on the child's `PATH` exactly as metaharness constructs it, reads its `--version`, and refuses a mismatch by name (`EVAL-RUN-017`) with both paths and both versions; an absent child `aep` is a printed warning.\n- A case whose `subject.skills` names `ess-schema:*` is refused (`EVAL-RUN-018`) when the child's `PATH` has no `ess`.\n- `--stream` ingestion is untouched; the test suite runs under a scratch `HOME` so a developer's own `home-path:sha256:8d6708581526e2954aab593f4ba61464fb67c0e06c88062276127839a99834b9` does not decide what it reports.\n- `task install` refreshes a real `home-path:sha256:cef90161b133031771c367dcbcdceb37a5db96829f01764e96ff21a7d794a49e` and `home-path:sha256:1704d3049436c375381628177c71498f26ecba8b00b31041de3473daa206b278` after the cargo install.\n","document":{"events":[],"fields":{"$aep":{"archived":false,"metadata":{"created_at":0,"id":"ent-cd8c75aafaf02f927a4bdbb8c5d534f5","locator":"ep://planning/store/story/eval-run-preflights-the-child-path","provenance":{"created_by":"system","updated_by":"system"},"revision":4,"type":"aep.story/v1","updated_at":0}},"body":"# Story: `aep eval run` refuses to spawn against a stale child `aep`\n\n## Outcome\n\nA live spawn is refused, before any money is spent, when the `aep` the session will execute is not the version that launched it; a case whose subject names an `ess-schema` skill is refused when the session has no `ess` to run.\n\n## Context\n\nmetaharness gives the session a constructed `PATH` — `home-path:sha256:bf0ce980507453a72ff552e629263aad96884f583e2ab5794252f4e5b2956f19` — and never the runner's own. On 2026-09-03 the golden-path case ran with a 0.40.1 copy in `home-path:sha256:8d6708581526e2954aab593f4ba61464fb67c0e06c88062276127839a99834b9` beside the 0.44.0 that launched it: step 3 was drafted by hand because `ess` was not there, and step 8 stopped at `aep doctor: unrecognized subcommand` after $10.96 had been spent. Nothing said the two binaries disagreed.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Before a live spawn the runner resolves `aep` on the child's `PATH` exactly as metaharness constructs it, reads its `--version`, and refuses a mismatch by name (`EVAL-RUN-017`) with both paths and both versions; an absent child `aep` is a printed warning.\n- A case whose `subject.skills` names `ess-schema:*` is refused (`EVAL-RUN-018`) when the child's `PATH` has no `ess`.\n- `--stream` ingestion is untouched; the test suite runs under a scratch `HOME` so a developer's own `home-path:sha256:8d6708581526e2954aab593f4ba61464fb67c0e06c88062276127839a99834b9` does not decide what it reports.\n- `task install` refreshes a real `home-path:sha256:cef90161b133031771c367dcbcdceb37a5db96829f01764e96ff21a7d794a49e` and `home-path:sha256:1704d3049436c375381628177c71498f26ecba8b00b31041de3473daa206b278` after the cargo install.\n","owner":"eval","relations":[{"decomposes":"epic:self-evaluation"},{"serves":"vision:O3"}],"status":"implemented","summary":"Resolve aep and ess on the PATH metaharness constructs for the session, compare versions, refuse a mismatch before any spend (EVAL-RUN-017/018).","tags":["bench","eval"],"title":"aep eval run refuses to spawn against a stale child aep"},"lifecycle_state":"implemented"},"owner":"eval","relations":[{"decomposes":"epic:self-evaluation"},{"serves":"vision:O3"}],"summary":"Resolve aep and ess on the PATH metaharness constructs for the session, compare versions, refuse a mismatch before any spend (EVAL-RUN-017/018).","tags":["bench","eval"],"title":"aep eval run refuses to spawn against a stale child aep"},"id":"ent-cd8c75aafaf02f927a4bdbb8c5d534f5","lifecycle_state":"implemented","revision":4,"version":1},"order":"per_kind_only","subject":["story","ent-cd8c75aafaf02f927a4bdbb8c5d534f5"]}]